{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:05:14.462Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\nSummary of what I did:\n\n1. **Created `src/core/status/dispatch-watch.ts`** — the watch primitive exporting `watchDispatch`, `WatchDispatchOptions`, `EveryFn`, `TreesFn`, `OnItems`, and `DispatchWatch`. It owns the invalidation hub, poll timer, tree-path refresh, and one-derivation-at-a-time queue; calls `onItems(items, at)` after each derivation; reports derivation failures via `options.stderr` as `osq inbox: <message>`; and `close()` cancels the poll, unsubscribes, closes the hub, and waits for the started run.\n\n2. **Rebuilt `src/core/status/dispatch-follow.ts`** on top of `watchDispatch`, keeping only the first `readDispatch` print, the `+`/`-` delta, and the sound. It still exports `followDispatch`, `FollowDispatchOptions`, and the re-exported `EveryFn`, so importers are unchanged.\n\n3. **Added `tests/dispatch-watch.test.ts`** covering every \"Dispatch watch\" scenario with a fake watcher, an immediate microtask scheduler, and a manual `every` timer.\n\nVerification:\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/dispatch-watch.test.ts`: 8/8 pass.\n- `tests/inbox-follow.test.ts`: 11/11 pass unchanged.\n- Full `pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, all 2445 CLI + 88 UI tests, lint): pass.\n- Result written to `openspec/changes/099-inbox-cards/.run/results/1.md`."}}
